---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import site from '../data/site.json';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Join the Steering Committee"
  description="Expressions of interest are welcome from researchers and practitioners who would like to help shape the future direction of ACM IMX."
>
  <div class="container page prose">
    <h1>Join the Steering Committee</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      The Steering Committee (SC) of the ACM International Conference on Interactive Media Experiences (IMX)
      welcomes expressions of interest from researchers and practitioners who would like to help shape the
      future direction of the conference.
    </p>

    <h2>About IMX</h2>
    <p>
      ACM IMX is the leading international conference for presentation and discussion of research into
      interactive media experiences. The conference brings together international researchers and
      practitioners from a wide range of disciplines, ranging from human-computer interaction, multimedia
      engineering and design to media studies, media psychology and sociology. IMX is sponsored by ACM SIGCHI,
      in cooperation with SIGMM and SIGWEB, and has its roots in EuroITV and ACM TVX.
    </p>

    <h2>Role of the Steering Committee</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Guiding the overall direction and vision of the conference</li>
      <li>Supporting and mentoring General Chairs and organising committees</li>
      <li>Reviewing and approving proposals to host future editions</li>
      <li>Maintaining conference policies, procedures and quality standards</li>
      <li>Promoting the conference and growing the community internationally</li>
      <li>Liaising with ACM and its Special Interest Groups</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Who should apply</h2>
    <p>
      We welcome expressions of interest from people with an active connection to the IMX community and a
      commitment to its growth. We are particularly interested in candidates who have:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>experience publishing at or organising IMX, or its predecessors TVX and EuroITV</li>
      <li>expertise in the conference's core research areas</li>
      <li>willingness to contribute time to meetings and tasks</li>
      <li>perspectives that broaden the diversity of the committee, including geography, discipline, career stage and background</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Prior senior organising experience is valued but not essential.</p>

    <h2>What to include</h2>
    <p>
      Please send an expression of interest of no more than one page to
      <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a>, including:
    </p>
    <ol>
      <li>your name, affiliation and role</li>
      <li>your involvement with the IMX community</li>
      <li>what you would bring to the committee and why you are interested</li>
      <li>relevant conference-organisation, community-building or service experience</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>Timeline</h2>
    <p>
      Expressions of interest are accepted at any time. New members are normally announced at the IMX
      conference each year.
    </p>

    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p>
      For informal enquiries, please contact the SC President via
      <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a>.
    </p>

    <p><em>
      IMX is committed to building an inclusive and welcoming community. We encourage expressions of interest
      from individuals of all backgrounds.
    </em></p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
